=== Summary ===
All 9 containers reached healthy after fixing a leftover-container network attachment issue (see README.md Architecture Verification).
Register -> cookie set (access Path=/, refresh Path=/auth) -> /auth/me via cookie -> refresh rotation via cookie -> reuse-detection 401 -> logout revokes + clears cookies -> refresh-after-logout 401 -> forgot/reset password -> old password 401, new password 200 -> change-password via Bearer -> final password 200: all verified against the real containerized Gateway+Identity+Postgres+Redis stack.
Rate limiting: window count carried over from the 4 prior /auth/login calls in this same script run within the 60s window; the 7th request in the dedicated loop (11th /auth/login call overall in that window) correctly received 429, matching RequestsPerWindow=10 with fixed-window semantics.
Fail-open: with Redis stopped, POST /auth/register still returned 201 (request allowed through), with a warning logged and the ADR 0007/0008 fail-open metric incremented. Redis was restarted afterward and the Gateway's aggregated /health returned Healthy again with no restart needed.
